        "source_symbol": "ordered_circular_filter",
        "description": "Sum weighted circular shifts in the supplied order, preserving float dtype. Nonempty finite float32/float64 arrays only. Axis is explicit and nonnegative; positive shifts move values toward increasing indices with wraparound. Shifts are integers and weights are finite real scalars representable in the input dtype. The first weighted shift initializes the result; later terms are added left to right without normalization or regrouping. Negative weights and repeated shifts are allowed. Reject nonfinite intermediate arithmetic. Returns a new array without changing caller inputs. Axis meanings, sampling intervals and filter interpretation belong to the caller; no domain policy.",
